---
import ItemPage from '../../layouts/ItemPage.astro';
import { CAKE_SIZES } from '../../data/cakes';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much is a Dairy Queen sheet cake?', a: 'A DQ sheet cake typically costs about $44.99. Prices vary by location and by design.' },
  { q: 'How many people does a DQ sheet cake feed?', a: 'About 20 to 25 people, depending on slice size.' },
  { q: 'How far ahead should I order a DQ sheet cake?', a: 'Plan on at least 48 hours. Sheet cakes are less likely to be waiting in the freezer case than round cakes.' },
  { q: 'Is a sheet cake cheaper per person than a round DQ cake?', a: 'Yes. At about $44.99 for 20 to 25 servings, it works out to about $1.80 to $2.25 per slice, the lowest of any DQ cake.' },
];
---
<ItemPage
  title="Dairy Queen Sheet Cake: Price & Servings (2026)"
  description="A Dairy Queen sheet cake costs about $44.99 and serves 20–25, the lowest price per slice of any DQ cake. Ordering, lead time and custom designs."
  name="Dairy Queen Sheet Cake"
  category={{ name: 'DQ Cakes', href: '/categories/dq-cakes' }}
  image="/Images/dq-sheet-cake.webp"
  imageAlt="Dairy Queen rectangular ice cream sheet cake"
  badges={['Serves 20–25', 'Best value per slice']}
  quick="A Dairy Queen sheet cake costs about $44.99 and serves 20 to 25 people, which works out to about $2 a slice. Order at least 48 hours ahead. Prices vary by location."
  from="From $44.99"
  intro="The sheet cake is DQ’s big-party option for classrooms, offices, sports teams and graduations. It has the same chocolate and vanilla soft serve and fudge crunch center as the round cakes, in a large rectangle."
  spec={[
    ['Price', '$44.99+'],
    ['Serves', '20–25 people'],
    ['Shape', 'Rectangular, about 11 × 14 inches'],
    ['Custom options', 'Message, colors and themed designs'],
    ['Lead time', 'At least 48 hours'],
  ]}
  allergens="Milk, Wheat, Soy"
  table={{ title: 'Compare DQ cake sizes and prices', ...CAKE_SIZES }}
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <h2>When a sheet cake makes sense</h2>
  <p>Choose a sheet cake when you have more than about 16 people. Two <a href="/items/dq-cake-round-10inch">10-inch cakes</a> would cost more and serve about the same number. For smaller groups, a round cake is easier to carry and store.</p>

  <h2>Ordering tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Order at least two days ahead, especially around graduations and holidays.</li>
    <li>Bring a cooler or drive straight to the party. A sheet cake softens fast in a warm car.</li>
    <li>Make sure your freezer has room before you pick it up.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For cutting and storage, see our <a href="/blog/dq-cakes-complete-guide">DQ cake serving guide</a>. All sizes are on the <a href="/categories/dq-cakes">DQ cake prices page</a>.</p>
</ItemPage>
